        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$853\\,374.94$\n\nStarting with $V_0=500\\,000$, iterate the supplied recurrence six times using Ans; round only the final balance.",
          "worked": "$\\begin{aligned}V_0&=500\\,000\\\\V_1&=500\\,000\\times1.1-4200=545\\,800\\\\V_2&=545\\,800\\times1.1-4200=596\\,180\\\\V_3&=596\\,180\\times1.1-4200=651\\,598\\\\V_4&=651\\,598\\times1.1-4200=712\\,557.8\\\\V_5&=712\\,557.8\\times1.1-4200=779\\,613.58\\\\V_6&=779\\,613.58\\times1.1-4200=853\\,374.938\\end{aligned}$\n\nThe balance after 6 payments is $\\$853\\,374.94$ to the nearest cent.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Explain why the value of the loan is increasing despite repayments.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The interest added each period exceeds the repayment, so the balance increases.",
          "worked": "The first period's interest is $0.10\\times500\\,000=\\$50\\,000$, which exceeds the $\\$4200$ repayment. As the balance increases, the interest also increases, so each repayment remains smaller than the interest added.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
